IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-nouns`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part1`

-- Tests for wa-interpretation-part1.l4 (ss 3(1), 3(2), 4).  Expected values are written from the text.

§ `Tests -- Part I`

-- s 3(1): applies to every written law, enacted before or after commencement, unless (a), (b) or (c).
#ASSERT `this Act applies to the written law` `an Act` (Date 1 1 1950) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `this Act applies to the written law` `an Act` (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `this Act applies to the written law` `subsidiary legislation` (Date 1 1 1950) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `this Act applies to the written law` `subsidiary legislation` (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (a) express provision to the contrary
#ASSERT NOT (`this Act applies to the written law` `an Act` (Date 1 1 2020) TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`this Act applies to the written law` `subsidiary legislation` (Date 1 1 2020) TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- (b) in the case of an Act, the intent and object, or the subject or context, is inconsistent
#ASSERT NOT (`this Act applies to the written law` `an Act` (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- (b) is about an Act only: it does not stop the Act applying to subsidiary legislation
#ASSERT `this Act applies to the written law` `subsidiary legislation` (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- (c) in the case of subsidiary legislation, the enabling Act's intent and object is inconsistent
#ASSERT NOT (`this Act applies to the written law` `subsidiary legislation` (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- (c) is about subsidiary legislation only
#ASSERT `this Act applies to the written law` `an Act` (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE TRUE

-- s 3(2) and s 4
#ASSERT `this Act is treated as an Act passed after its own commencement`
#ASSERT `the Crown is bound by this Act`
